WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.781
Here's why this matters: the series
moves four populations to the cloud,

2
00:00:04.781 --> 00:00:08.288
each on its own track, and
this session is the HR track.

3
00:00:08.288 --> 00:00:09.412
It's about people.

4
00:00:09.412 --> 00:00:12.972
Employees come from Core HCM,
and contractors from the

5
00:00:12.972 --> 00:00:16.612
contractor source of authority
the agency designates.

6
00:00:16.612 --> 00:00:21.299
Those attributes land on the user
object, in AD while users are synced,

7
00:00:21.299 --> 00:00:24.669
then in Entra ID, and
groups, administrative units,

8
00:00:24.669 --> 00:00:28.451
Conditional Access and
Lifecycle Workflows read them.

9
00:00:28.451 --> 00:00:32.295
You're there when every enabled
account matches an authoritative

10
00:00:32.295 --> 00:00:36.350
record or an owned exception, and no
hand-kept group membership is left.

11
00:00:36.350 --> 00:00:40.978
Devices, servers, service accounts
and AI agents are other books;

12
00:00:40.978 --> 00:00:42.725
HR never describes them.

13
00:00:42.725 --> 00:00:45.380
Next, why the data matters so much now.
